{"name":"Roselle","hex":"#f0dee4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Roselle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Roselle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mike Roselle","blocks":[{"text":"Mike Roselle is an American environmental activist and author who is a prominent member of the radical environmentalism movement. Roselle is one of the co-founders of the radical environmental organization Earth First!, as well as of Rainforest Action Network, the Ruckus Society, and Climate Ground Zero."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Roselle","wikidata":"Q6848624"},{"title":"Roselle Nava","blocks":[{"text":"Roselle Paulino Nava-Tan is a Filipino singer, film and television actress, and former politician. She is a multi-platinum female singer in the Philippines and one of the most in-demand divas during the '90s era. She is tagged as the \"Philippines' Sentimental Diva\" and the \"former supreme songbird of ABS-CBN\". She was formerly dubbed as the \"90s Philippine Pop Queen\". She started her career as a part of ABS-CBN's defunct youth-oriented show Ang TV (1992–1997) together with Jolina Magdangal, Claudine Barretto, Antoinette Taus, etc. She was also a regular host and performer of ASAP, the Philippines longest variety show, from 1995 to 2004 and since 2015."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roselle_Nava","wikidata":"Q15279156"},{"title":"Roselle (plant)","blocks":[{"text":"Roselle is a species of flowering plant in the family Malvaceae, likely native to parts of Africa. In the 16th and early 17th centuries it was spread to Asia and the West Indies, where it has since become naturalized in many places. The stems are used for the production of bast fibre and the calyces are commonly steeped to make an infusion popular in many places around the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Roselle%2C_Hibiscus_sabdariffa%2C_2014_01.JPG/330px-Roselle%2C_Hibiscus_sabdariffa%2C_2014_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roselle_(plant)","wikidata":"Q319390"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Roselle_%28Hibiscus_sabdariffa%29.png/500px-Roselle_%28Hibiscus_sabdariffa%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Roselle_%28Hibiscus_sabdariffa%29.png/500px-Roselle_%28Hibiscus_sabdariffa%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Capsule","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoselle_(Hibiscus_sabdariffa).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Roselle_2%2C_Hibiscus_sabdariffa%2C_2014.JPG/500px-Roselle_2%2C_Hibiscus_sabdariffa%2C_2014.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Roselle_2%2C_Hibiscus_sabdariffa%2C_2014.JPG/1280px-Roselle_2%2C_Hibiscus_sabdariffa%2C_2014.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Roselle_2%2C_Hibiscus_sabdariffa%2C_2014.JPG/500px-Roselle_2%2C_Hibiscus_sabdariffa%2C_2014.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wave Hill","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoselle_2%2C_Hibiscus_sabdariffa%2C_2014.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Roselle_%28Hibiscus_sabdariffa%29_fruits.jpg/500px-Roselle_%28Hibiscus_sabdariffa%29_fruits.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Roselle_%28Hibiscus_sabdariffa%29_fruits.jpg/1280px-Roselle_%28Hibiscus_sabdariffa%29_fruits.jp